{"description":"`eka sync` (push) advances the repository snapshot — adding, removing or retyping stratum-1/2 units changes the constraint index — but it does NOT regenerate the managed AGENTS.md block. A repository that carries the block (the M0 `agents-md` surface) is therefore left drifted after any knowledge sync that touches the index. Observed on develop: the knowledge sync cf0e014 added `dec:m3a-verify-staging` and `dec:code-discover-symlink-fix` (and `spec:add-specification-overview`), and merging the M0 PR on top produced AGENTS.md drift that made `eka verify` (the M3a CI gate) exit 1 on develop. The gate caught it correctly; the block needed a manual `eka agents-md --write`. The step is manual today: there is no automatic regeneration on sync push, no warning, and the drift only surfaces through the gate or `agents-md --check`.","impact":"Every knowledge sync that changes the index turns the CI quality gate red on the syncing branch until someone runs `eka agents-md --write` and commits it — a maintenance step that is easy to forget and lands as a separate commit after the fact. It also makes the M0 drift gate look like a false positive to a reader who did not perform the sync. No data is corrupted (the snapshot is authoritative), but the develop gate fails transiently and the AGENTS.md block is stale on any branch that does not regenerate."}